WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.920
Preparation happens before the alert that everyone remembers.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.503
It is the quiet work that makes the rest of incident response possible:

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:11.028
assigning roles, defining escalation paths, maintaining playbooks, confirming tool access,

00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:15.610
checking log availability, testing backups, and making sure decision makers can be reached.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.783
Preparation also includes legal, privacy, communications, and business-owner coordination,

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:21.250
because many incidents are not purely technical.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.070
A suspicious login may affect an employee account,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.890
a cloud credential exposure may involve customer data,

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.063
and a system outage may require business continuity decisions.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:34.293
The team should know who can approve containment, who can contact vendors,

00:00:34.293 --> 00:00:38.170
who can speak to leadership, and where evidence should be stored.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:43.458
Tabletop exercises and drills are useful because they expose gaps before a real incident does.

00:00:43.458 --> 00:00:47.335
A playbook that has never been tested is only a theory.

00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:50.860
Readiness means people understand their role, monitoring provides useful context,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.090
backups can actually be restored, and communication paths work when time matters.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.558
Good preparation lowers confusion, shortens response time,

00:00:57.558 --> 00:01:00.730
and gives responders confidence that they can act safely.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:05.312
A practical readiness review should also check boring details that become critical later:

00:01:05.312 --> 00:01:08.838
who can approve emergency access, where bridge notes are kept,

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:10.953
which logs are retained long enough,

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:15.183
and how the team reaches a vendor or cloud provider after hours.

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:19.060
Preparation turns those details into known paths instead of last-minute discoveries.
